WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
The Ebola outbreak in the Democratic Republic of Congo has now passed 12,000 confirmed cases.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:14.000
Government data released on Thursday puts the total at 12,021 infections with 5,904 deaths.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:19.040
The outbreak was declared in mid-May in a turi province in the northeast of the country

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:25.520
and has since spread to eight of Congo's 26 provinces. It is caused by a rare strain of the virus

00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:31.040
called Bundibugyo for which there is no approved vaccine or treatment. Fighting between the army

00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:36.400
and rebels in the east is disrupting the response. Health workers have been evacuated from some

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:42.560
areas and only about 15% of new cases are among known contacts of infected people,

00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:48.000
which means many chains of transmission are being missed. It is now the second largest Ebola

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:53.360
outbreak on record, behind only the West African outbreak of 2014 to 2016.

